<!DOCTYPE html>
<%!-- No safe-area-x on <html> — that would inset the WHOLE app so the 3-column
     rails couldn't reach the screen edge. Safe insets live on the rail content
     (safe-pl / safe-pr) and on full-bleed single-column page roots instead, so
     backgrounds go edge-to-edge while content clears the notch / dynamic island. --%>
<html lang="en" class="h-full bg-brand-paper dark:bg-brand-ink">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <%!-- Base viewport. JS below adds maximum-scale=1 on iOS only to
         prevent auto-zoom on input focus. iOS ignores it for pinch-zoom
         (safe). Android respects it (blocks pinch-zoom = bad), so we
         only set it where it's needed. --%>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <script>
      if (/iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(navigator.userAgent)) {
        document.querySelector('meta[name=viewport]').setAttribute('content',
          'width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover');
      }
    </script>
    <%!-- PWA / add-to-home-screen. `standalone` (manifest + apple meta) launches
         chromeless like a native app; the apple-touch-icon is the home-screen
         icon on iOS (which ignores manifest icons); the title is the label under
         it. theme-color tints the status bar / title bar to match the shell. --%>
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#18181b" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="loopyard" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/icon-180.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/icons/icon.svg" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <title>
      Loopyard - An open-source multiplayer software factory where humans and AI ship code together.
    </title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/app.css"} />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/app.js"}>
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="h-full antialiased font-sans">
    <%!-- Connection-lost banner. Hidden by default; the LiveSocket lifecycle in
    app.js reveals it when the websocket has been down past a short grace period,
    so you always know when a send won't go through (the input also holds the text
    until the server acks — see the ChatForm hook). --%>
    <div
      id="conn-banner"
      role="status"
      aria-live="polite"
      class="hidden fixed top-0 inset-x-0 z-[100] flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-amber-500 text-amber-950 text-sm font-medium px-4 py-1.5 shadow-md safe-pt"
    >
      <%!-- Terse status, one line, no wrap: pulsing dot = actively reconnecting;
           sends queue meanwhile (ChatForm holds text until the ack). --%>
      <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-900 animate-pulse flex-none"></span>
      <span class="truncate">Disconnected — reconnecting…</span>
      <button
        type="button"
        onclick="window.location.reload()"
        class="underline underline-offset-2 font-semibold hover:opacity-80 flex-none whitespace-nowrap"
      >
        Reload
      </button>
    </div>
    <a
      href="#main-content"
      class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:fixed focus:top-2 focus:left-2 focus:z-50 focus:bg-violet-600 focus:text-white focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:rounded-md focus:font-medium"
    >
      Skip to main content
    </a>
    <%!-- Ambient audio ENGINE — the "room tone" of Loopyard. Lives in the root
         layout (outside {@inner_content}); the whole app runs in one
         live_session, so it's mounted once and the bed keeps playing across
         every navigation. No visible control here — the speaker button + settings
         panel live in the page headers (`<.operator_link>`) and drive this engine
         over window events. Streams the `activity` channel, which ActivitySound
         drives from live agent events. --%>
    <%!-- phx-update="ignore": the engine sets the <audio> `src` in JS, so
         LiveView must NEVER diff this subtree — otherwise morphdom compares
         against the server markup (which has no src), strips the src, and the
         audio stops mid-play (looked like a cutoff + flipped to "muted" when
         switching tracks). Ignoring it keeps the stream alive across every
         render and navigation. --%>
    <%!-- `hidden`: this is the audio ENGINE, never a visible control. Without it,
         the <audio> (no `controls`) can still render a small replaced-element
         sliver in some browsers — a block in the body flow ABOVE the app, which
         showed as a white gap at the top of every page. Audio plays fine while
         display:none, so hiding it costs nothing and reclaims the space. --%>
    <div id="ambient" phx-hook="AmbientAudio" phx-update="ignore" data-channel="activity" class="hidden">
      <audio id="ambient-el" preload="none"></audio>
    </div>
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
